                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "238473753",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198859708131",
                            "num_reviews": 214,
                            "playtime_forever": 176,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 111,
                            "playtime_at_review": 64,
                            "last_played": 1794072769
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Good concept, mediocre execution. The biggest issue with this game is that the most interesting part of the game is the horror segments but they take up the least amount of the gameplay. Most of the gameplay is just your normal duck hunt stuff, but the shotgun is incredibly uncomfortable to hold and your left hand can’t actually grab the pump. You just have to vaguely hover your hand where it should be, which means that pumping the shotgun is always inconsistent. I had to mess around with controller offsets in the steam VR settings because by default, the shotgun points very high up, which meant that I had to uncomfortably bend my wrist to be able to have a chance of hitting anything, even after setting offsets it was still uncomfortable as a whole. I wouldn’t recommend the game unless you’re just a big fan of stress level zero and wanted to see this part of VR history.",
